<http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/assertion> {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-esmfold-P81459-esmatlas> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-esmfold-P81459-esmatlas> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "ESMFold v1, called through Meta's public ESM Atlas endpoint, returned a predicted structure for Cytochrome c from Thunnus alalunga (UniProt P81459, 103 residues) with mean pLDDT 93 and 100% of residues at pLDDT 70 or above." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-esmfold-P81459-esmatlas> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "A model output, not a measurement. The sequence was taken from a checksummed UniProt record, sent to a hosted ESMFold service, and the returned coordinates were kept with their checksum. pLDDT is the model's own per-residue confidence; the file reports it on a 0 to 1 scale and the numbers here are that column multiplied by 100, which the run record states. No experimental structure of this protein was fetched or compared, so nothing here is validated against a measurement." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-esmfold-P81459-esmatlas> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hypothesisType> "model output (predicted structure)" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-esmfold-P81459-esmatlas> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Protein Cytochrome c, Thunnus alalunga (NCBITaxon:8235), residues 1-103 of UniProt P81459 version 1. Service ESM Atlas public API (Meta; not BioNeMo), endpoint https://api.esmatlas.com/foldSequence/v1/pdb/, 2026-10-31T06:41:36.655Z. One prediction, no sampling, no relaxation, no template." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-esmfold-P81459-esmatlas> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasEvidence> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/organism-esmfold-P81459-esmatlas-run> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-esmfold-P81459-esmatlas> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/proposedTest> "Superpose the prediction on an experimental structure of this protein from the PDB and report CA RMSD per residue against pLDDT. High pLDDT where the superposition is poor would show the confidence is miscalibrated for this family." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-esmfold-P81459-esmatlas> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Does not establish: the structure of this protein. A predicted structure is not a measured one, and pLDDT is the model's confidence, not its accuracy. The prediction was not compared with any experimental structure." .
}
<http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/provenance> {
  <http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/assertion> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasAttributedTo> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-organism-esmfold-client> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-organism-esmfold-client> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#SoftwareAgent> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-organism-esmfold-client> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "organism-design/esmfold/smoke-test.mjs: calls a hosted ESMFold service on one checksummed UniProt sequence and records what happened." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-organism-esmfold-client> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "organism-design/esmfold/smoke-test.mjs" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-organism-esmfold-client> <https://schema.org/codeRepository> <https://github.com/fractastical/delphi> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-organism-esmfold-client> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/usesModel> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/esmfold-v1> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/esmfold-v1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LanguageModel> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/esmfold-v1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "ESMFold v1, a protein language model with a structure head" .
